WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.510
(music)

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:06.120
I would say the honors co-op program made
it possible for me to have the career

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.720
I have now.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.639
Um. I really was an electrical engineer, and that's all I was when I got out of

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:13.580
undergraduate school.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:18.270
Um. I don't think I would have been able
to succeed in with essentially a

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.960
undergraduate school.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.560
Um. I don't think I would have been able
to succeed in what's essentially a

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.769
software career,

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:29.289
um, had I not done the honors co-op
program.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.220
This honors co-op program really benefited
me professionally because

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:37.329
I was able to get some exposure to what
the business world is like.

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:41.180
And found out that's something I like to do.
And subsequently,

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.699
at least at Xerox, I was able to move away
from an engineering career path, to, um,

00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:48.600
moving to the strategic business office.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.800
The honors co-op program had a very deep impact on my professional development, ah,

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.859
because it really gave me the skills
that ah I need to do my job today,

00:00:56.859 --> 00:01:00.379
which is no longer pure engineering, but a
much broader

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:04.000
sense of whole business management.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.920
I, as a hiring manager, and, ah, am looking for talent, when I see a
Stanford Master's degree

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.970
on that resume, first of all, I know what it
means to get one.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.240
And I actually put on my resume not only
that I got my master's degree, but I also

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.899
did it during the time when I was working.

00:01:19.909 --> 00:01:28.000
(silence)

